course: dictionary
lesson: 889
title: Birdwatch: a verb and a noun
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A verb tells you what someone does, and a noun names a thing or an event. Birdwatch can be both. To birdwatch is to watch wild birds as a hobby. A birdwatch is an organised event where people watch and count birds together.
explain: Use the words around it to choose the right meaning. In «Citizen scientists are ordinary people who count birds, butterflies and frogs and send the numbers to scientists», the clue is count: the people are watching and counting animals, so the word is about nature and numbers.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Ella likes to birdwatch in the garden, so birdwatch is a verb, an action. The school joined a birdwatch in the park, so birdwatch is a noun, an event. Ask yourself: is someone doing it, or is it a thing that happens?
fact: To birdwatch means to watch wild birds in their natural surroundings, often with binoculars and a bird book.
fact: A birdwatch is an organised event where people watch and count birds.
fact: Birdwatching helps children learn bird names, songs and the places where birds live.
fact: The RSPB's Big Garden Birdwatch in the UK asks families to count birds for one hour, and the results help scientists.
fact: Similar counts happen in the USA, Canada, Australia and New Zealand. A keen birdwatcher is someone who loves this hobby.
exercise: What does to birdwatch mean? | To cook birds for dinner | To draw pictures of trees | *To watch wild birds in their natural surroundings as a hobby | To chase birds away from the garden
exercise: In «The school joined a birdwatch in the park», what kind of word is birdwatch? | A question word | *A noun, an organised event | A verb, an action | A describing word
exercise: Ella likes to ___ in the garden with her binoculars. Which word fits? | sing | count | hide | *birdwatch
test: What is the Big Garden Birdwatch? | A film about the ocean | A race to see who can run fastest | *An organised count where families count birds for one hour | A lesson about fish in the sea
test: Who is a keen birdwatcher? | A person who sells birdseed | *Someone who loves watching birds as a hobby | A bird that sings very loudly | Someone who never leaves the house
exam: Which sentence uses birdwatch as a verb? | *«Please birdwatch quietly, children, so the robins stay calm.» | «Our birdwatch will start at nine o'clock.» | «The class took part in a birdwatch and counted robins.» | «The birdwatch in the park was busy this morning.»
